From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jacob McSwain <jacob@mcswain.dev>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:07:28 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gateway): socket tickets outlive a restart handover

gateway.restart_ticket_handover (false = off): just before a restart releases the profile, the stopping gateway writes its unused, unexpired socket tickets to $HERMES_HOME/.ws-ticket-handover.json (mode 0600), and the gateway that takes the profile over loads them before its listener opens and removes the file. A dial with a ticket the old gateway minted, relayed or forwarded to the new one, opens instead of being refused with 403 or 1008. Tickets keep their expiry and stay single-use.
---
